\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Headline reversal under the released evaluator and its absence across recipe reconstructions. (a) System scores under the released evaluator (sacreBLEU-4, canonical 641-query protocol): TN-PURE 23.02 vs.\ REC 12.78 ($\Delta =+10.24$, post-selected descriptive 95\% CI $[8.87,11.64]$), with TN-PTCOMP 18.86, PT 1.59, oracle-gloss PURE 11.4, and random-donor PURE 0.90 (seeds 0--19, $\pm $1 SD). (b) Per-checkpoint PURE$-$REC gaps: released evaluator ($+10.24$) vs.\ fourteen \emph  {paper-derived} (legacy) recipe reconstructions (seeds 101--1405), all 14 negative (donor-cluster bootstrap 95\% CIs; descriptive seed dispersion range $[-1.85,-0.80]$, all 14 values below zero). The 10 step-corrected and 16 joint-loss families are shown in Fig.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:competence}; none of them produces a positive gap either (see Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:accounting}). All reconstructions are less competent than the released evaluator; the figure demonstrates non-replication within the constructible family, not an isolated causal checkpoint effect.\relax }}{17}{figure.caption.35}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:headline}{{1}{17}{Headline reversal under the released evaluator and its absence across recipe reconstructions. (a) System scores under the released evaluator (sacreBLEU-4, canonical 641-query protocol): TN-PURE 23.02 vs.\ REC 12.78 ($\Delta =+10.24$, post-selected descriptive 95\% CI $[8.87,11.64]$), with TN-PTCOMP 18.86, PT 1.59, oracle-gloss PURE 11.4, and random-donor PURE 0.90 (seeds 0--19, $\pm $1 SD). (b) Per-checkpoint PURE$-$REC gaps: released evaluator ($+10.24$) vs.\ fourteen \emph {paper-derived} (legacy) recipe reconstructions (seeds 101--1405), all 14 negative (donor-cluster bootstrap 95\% CIs; descriptive seed dispersion range $[-1.85,-0.80]$, all 14 values below zero). The 10 step-corrected and 16 joint-loss families are shown in Fig.~\ref {fig:competence}; none of them produces a positive gap either (see Table~\ref {tab:accounting}). All reconstructions are less competent than the released evaluator; the figure demonstrates non-replication within the constructible family, not an isolated causal checkpoint effect.\relax }{figure.caption.35}{}}
